# Frontend Development Rules

## Technology Stack
- React with TypeScript
- Vite for build tooling
- Shadcn for UI components
- dndkit for drag and drop functionality
- TanStack Router for routing
- LegendState for state management
- Supabase for backend integration

## Project Structure
```
frontend/
├── src/
│   ├── components/     # Reusable UI components
│   ├── features/       # Feature-specific components and logic
│   ├── hooks/         # Custom React hooks
│   ├── lib/           # Utility functions and configurations
│   ├── public/        # Static assets
│   ├── state/         # LegendState stores
│   ├── styles/        # Global styles and themes
│   ├── routes/        # File Routing Componenets
│   └── types/         # TypeScript type definitions
```

## Development Guidelines

### State Management
- Use LegendState for complex state management
- Leverage IndexedDB for local storage
- Implement cloud sync with Supabase
- Keep state updates atomic and predictable

### UI/UX Principles
- Follow Figma design specifications
- Implement responsive design patterns
- Desktop-first development with mobile adaptations
- Clear loading and error states
- Accessible color schemes and contrast ratios

### Mobile Considerations
- List view for course planning on small screens
- Touch-friendly interface elements
- Clear messaging about desktop features
- Optimized performance for mobile devices

### Performance
- Implement code splitting
- Optimize bundle size
- Use lazy loading for routes
- Efficient re-rendering strategies

### Testing
- Unit tests for utility functions
- Component testing with React Testing Library
- E2E testing for critical user flows
- Accessibility testing

### Code Style
- Follow TypeScript best practices
- Use Biome for formatting and linting
- Maintain consistent component structure
- Document complex logic and components

### Security
- Store sensitive data in environment variables
- Implement proper CORS policies
- Secure user data handling
- Input validation and sanitization

## Feature Implementation

### Course Planning
- Drag and drop interface for desktop
- List-based interface for mobile
- Real-time prerequisite checking
- Visual semester organization

### Data Management
- Automatic saving to IndexedDB
- Optional Supabase sync
- Import/Export functionality
- Data validation

### User Experience
- Clear error messages
- Loading states
- Undo/Redo functionality
- Responsive feedback

## Build and Deployment
- Environment-specific configurations
- Production build optimization
- Error tracking and monitoring
- Performance metrics tracking

## Command Line
- When installing new packages or running node commands where'd you usuall use `npm`, or `npx`. Use `bun` and `bunx` insteadd.